solution:
\(A = Z + N\)  \(\therefore Z = A - N\)

For the given three elements \(A = 40\). Values of their atomic numbers \(Z\), are obtained from the given values of neutron numbers, \(N\), using the above expression.

for Q : \(Z = A - N = 40 - 22 = 18\)

for R : \(Z = A - N = 40 - 21 = 19\)

for T : \(Z = A - N = 40 - 20 = 20\)

\(\therefore\) The atomic composition of the three elements is written as follows :

\(^{40}_{18}\mathrm{Q}\), \(^{40}_{19}\mathrm{R}\), \(^{40}_{20}\mathrm{T}\)
